# FERNHILL BANK: RISK COMMITTEE PACK

Board risk committee, Thursday 8 January 2026.
Position at 31 December 2025; produced by Ballast.

## 1 Headline

- CET1 is 16.7% against a target of 16.0%: inside appetite, $40.9m
  above the target. The $543.1m above the requirement is not spare.
- The supervisor's scenario takes CET1 to -2.1%, below its tolerance
  of 4.5%. The watchlist (grades 9-10, $1,078.9m of exposure) is the
  cause; the scenario can carry $283.3m of it.
- Economic capital is 78.4% of CET1 against a ceiling of 73.0%.
- The commercial book returns -0.4% on its capital before running
  costs; retail returns 45.9%.
- Of 14 appetite metrics, 7 are red, 3 amber and 4 green.

